How many questions from Magnetic Effect of Current appear in JEE Advanced each year?

Typically 1 to 3 questions appear per paper from this chapter. Over the 2009-2026 window, the chapter averaged approximately 2 questions per year across both papers. The format alternates between Integer type, multi-correct MCQ, and Matrix-Match, making it one of the more format-varied chapters in JEE Advanced Physics.

Is the Magnetic Effect of Current chapter important for JEE Main as well?

Yes. JEE Main tests the same chapter but at a lower difficulty level - mostly single-correct MCQs on standard configurations like a circular loop at its centre or a solenoid. If you can solve JEE Advanced problems from this chapter, JEE Main questions become straightforward. Build your preparation on JEE Advanced PYQs and JEE Main questions will follow naturally.

What is the best way to solve the cylindrical cavity problem using superposition?

Treat the system as a complete solid cylinder (radius 2a, current density J) minus a smaller solid cylinder (the cavity, radius a). Calculate the magnetic field at point P from each cylinder separately using Ampere's law, treating each as carrying the same current density J. Then subtract the field vectors. The answer for the 2012 JEE Advanced problem gives N = 5.

Why do an electron and proton exit a magnetic field region at different times even at the same speed?

The time spent inside a semi-infinite magnetic field region equals the arc length divided by speed, which equals (πm)/(qB) - half the cyclotron period. Since the proton mass is ~1836 times the electron mass, the proton takes ~1836 times longer to complete its semicircle. Speed is irrelevant to exit time; only mass and charge determine it.

How should I use previous year JEE Advanced questions in my study plan?

First, study the theory and solved examples from your primary material. Then attempt each PYQ independently under timed conditions (8-10 minutes per question for multi-correct, 5-7 minutes for Integer type). After checking the answer, identify which concept was tested - not just whether you got it right. Build a concept-error log. eSaral's 5-layer doubt-solving system ensures that every unresolved doubt from a PYQ gets answered before your next revision cycle. Leave a comment
