How many questions from Wave on String appear in JEE Advanced each year?

Typically 1-2 questions per paper from the Waves chapter appear in JEE Advanced. Over the 2011-2018 period, 9 questions were asked across both papers. Sub-topics with highest frequency are Doppler effect and resonance column experiments. This makes Waves a high-priority chapter for JEE Advanced preparation.

Is the Doppler effect important for JEE Advanced or just JEE Main?

Doppler effect is important for both JEE Main and JEE Advanced, but JEE Advanced questions are more complex - often involving reflection, two-step Doppler analysis, or geometric arrangements with moving observers. Three of the nine Waves questions in this collection directly test Doppler effect, confirming its importance.

How do I identify whether a resonance corresponds to a fundamental or a higher harmonic?

Calculate λ/4 from the known speed and frequency. Then check if the given length is a close match to λ/4 (fundamental), 3λ/4 (1st overtone / 3rd harmonic), or 5λ/4 (2nd overtone). In the JEE Advanced 2018 question, 50.$7\text{ cm}$ ≈ 3 × 16.$6\text{ cm}$ = 49.$8\text{ cm}$, confirming the 3rd harmonic - not the fundamental. Always verify numerically. Leave a comment
